{"id": "EUVD-2026-80504", "enisaUuid": "d49c1ef7-2707-33c3-a7c8-d75638e7dab9", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nLoongArch: Fix acpi_package_ids[] array overflow\n\nWith LoongArch virt machine, a typical setting is one core per socket,\nthere will max 256 sockets (packages) on one VM. With PPTT acpi table,\narray acpi_package_ids[] will be overflowed.\n\nHere change the array size of acpi_package_ids[] with the max value of\nMAX_PACKAGES and KVM_MAX_VCPUS.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:32:03", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:54:37", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0195e04b1eec8fb00e2db9c5e55655a3f5e76f60", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d3fd094c13c6d0b74f246461ca4cf427d539c8e8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6311b8c471afa33c18adbe4eb16f862936b71ca3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2a2367d46d7a4ee4122b7a86e57125542dbbe963"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f448-wjgg-crg4", "CVE-2026-89904"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b40575e-51e2-3161-a72b-7e6e24f3723a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.101 <6.12.110"}, {"id": "0cc01553-0f89-356d-91ac-c3ce4a48cba8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18.42 <6.18.51"}, {"id": "20a12442-a26e-3b8f-aee9-4879bdc03306", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4427a33faabb4b81511b99dfee18ce0a38b5b5df <d3fd094c13c6d0b74f246461ca4cf427d539c8e8"}, {"id": "22d62274-43bd-3296-84e0-b88636004c5d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.1.6 <7.2"}, {"id": "4a70be3e-ab9d-3490-a165-f4a95a94519d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "56446f42-3776-3157-845d-5d1d880e0288", "product": {"name": "Linux", "ve